WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.976
Today’s lesson goal: Today’s lesson goal: make decisions with if, elif, and else. Compare values and combine conditions. Repeat work with for and while loops.

2
00:00:12.826 --> 00:00:27.802
Why control flow matters: Why control flow matters. Programs choose paths for discounts, menus, and checks. Loops process lists without copy-paste. This is the logic behind everyday apps.

3
00:00:28.652 --> 00:00:42.884
Decisions: if / elif / else: Decisions use if, elif, and else. Ask a true or false question. Run one branch when the answer is true. Use elif for more cases, and else for the rest.

4
00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:59.502
Worked example: discount: Worked example: a discount. If spend is over one hundred, apply ten percent. Elif spend is over fifty, apply five percent. Otherwise no discount — print the final total.

5
00:01:00.352 --> 00:01:12.496
Loops: for and while: Loops: use for to walk through a known collection. Use while to keep going until a condition changes. Avoid infinite loops — always update the condition.

6
00:01:13.346 --> 00:01:26.882
Common mistakes: Common mistakes: using a single equals instead of double equals in comparisons. Forgetting indentation under if or for. While true with no break or stop condition.

7
00:01:27.732 --> 00:01:40.500
Practice checkpoint: Practice checkpoint: build a tiny menu or age check. Loop through a short list and print each item. Then continue in the written Module 3 lesson and quiz.
